From d723b533b9cd7849f2c92abad02f6d6bf7c10bd6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: BellSoft <info@bell-sw.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 22:24:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] osvlocal: sources of the vendor databases, warn when one is
 unavailable

Settings for the ecosystem families of the vendor's products (the
module's Ecosystems: its two distributions and the standalone JDK and
NIK); no other ecosystem changes. They have no field in the plugin's proto
config and are set with the new Configure(Options).

* Archive location (archiveURL): Options.VendorFeeds[family] (a base or
  the .zip itself; ParseVendorFeeds reads "<family>=<location>" pairs),
  else Options.VendorURL (<url>/<family>/all.zip; http(s), file:// or a
  directory), else the built-in default: the archive host (osv.dev bucket
  or its mirror) for the distributions, the module's product base URL for
  the standalone runtimes, which the osv.dev bucket does not carry.
* Options.LocalOnlyEcosystems: match only the ecosystems api.osv.dev does
  not serve and download their archives. A scan that queries api.osv.dev
  runs the enricher this way next to vulnmatch/osvdev.
* An archive of a vendor family that cannot be obtained is one warning per
  family (osvdata.UnavailableError.Warning):

    <vendor> OSV data for "<family>" is unavailable (<reason>); packages of
    this product were NOT checked against <vendor> advisories. Source: <url>

  The packages stay in the inventory without findings and the other
  packages are matched. Options.VendorStrict keeps it an error.
